# The controls, played through the client as a person would: select the
# base, narrow to a type with its tile, place a structure through the build
# grid's tabs, queue units, give orders, and cancel prompts. Positions are
# pixels in the 1600 x 900 window; the camera starts over blue's base.
at 0.5 shot start
at 1.0 drag 450,200 1150,700            # the base: the factory and its engineers
at 1.2 expect selected >= 3
at 1.3 shot base
# Builders (the selection has engineers): the build grid has the grid keys.
at 1.5 key Q                            # economy, first item: an extractor to place
at 1.6 expect busy == 1
at 1.7 key Escape                       # cancels the placement, doesn't leave the zone
at 1.8 expect busy == 0
at 2.0 key V                            # the build tab
at 2.1 key Q                            # a factory
at 2.2 shot placing
at 2.3 click 640,300                    # put it down
at 2.5 expect sent build == 1
at 2.6 expect busy == 0
# Orders are live whatever's selected: stop, then move with a click.
at 2.8 key Space
at 2.9 expect sent stop == 1
at 3.0 key M
at 3.1 expect busy == 1
at 3.2 click 900,420
at 3.4 expect sent move == 1
at 3.5 key G                            # fight, then cancelled
at 3.6 key Escape
at 3.7 expect busy == 0
at 3.8 expect sent fight == 0
# Narrow to the factory with its tile (the second: types in order), then produce.
at 4.0 click 170,750
at 4.2 expect selected == 1
at 4.3 shot factory
at 4.4 key Q                            # a raider
at 4.5 key W shift                      # five tanks
at 4.7 expect sent produce == 2
at 4.8 key Y                            # repeat on
at 4.9 expect sent repeat == 1
at 5.0 key X                            # the logistics page
at 5.1 shot logistics
at 5.3 expect selected == 1
at 5.4 drag 450,200 1150,700             # builders again: their own tab, not the factory's page
at 5.45 key Q                            # economy's first item, still
at 5.47 expect busy == 1
at 5.48 key Escape
# A factory started, then stopped: a right-click on the unfinished site resumes it.
at 5.5 key V
at 5.55 key Q
at 5.6 click 770,560
at 5.7 expect sent build == 2
at 11.0 key Space
at 11.1 shot unfinished
at 11.2 click 770,560 right
at 11.4 expect sent build == 3
at 11.5 expect sent fight == 0           # not a fight order on the ground
# A drag while placing lays out a grid: generators, a block of them.
at 11.7 key Z                           # the economy tab
at 11.8 key W                           # a generator
at 11.9 drag 1000,560 1150,660
at 12.1 shot grid
at 12.2 expect sent build >= 9          # 3 before, and the grid's
at 12.3 expect busy == 0
at 12.4 key Escape                      # nothing in progress: leaves (here, quits)
at 13.4 expect sent any >= 15           # never reached if Escape left
